  "audio": "025.because-handing-a.mp3",
  "paragraph": 25,
  "text": "Because handing a language model a shell tool means granting arbitrary code execution, verification must pair with hard physical containment. Production harnesses like Codex, Devin, OpenHands, and GitHub Copilot Coding Agent run untrusted commands inside ephemeral Docker containers, lightweight microVMs, or OS-level sandboxes such as macOS Seatbelt and Linux bubblewrap. Those walls enforce strict writable-directory boundaries and block unauthorized network egress, ensuring that even a hallucinated shell command or prompt injection cannot wreck your host machine or exfiltrate private credentials.",
